  "limits": [
    "Publisher-linked auction ABIs and v1.1 adaptation authenticate retained events, not independent source/bytecode equivalence or universal routing. Removed error interfaces are not events.",
    "No reviewed AuctionEnded, SoldOut or timestamp-bearing round event exists in these auction interfaces. Missing definitions are not invented.",
    "DayRolled may be observed in a later transaction; its block time does not by itself establish the scheduled opening or expiry. A purchase timestamp establishes execution, not opening.",
    "Historical duration, applied cap, half-life, payment semantics and configuration transitions need interval-specific evidence; current getters and whitepaper constants cannot substitute.",
    "License day identifiers may restart across deployments; grouping must include the exact emitting address. The helper scans legacy over the full requested interval and v1.1 from its creation block, including the pre-cutover initialization interval. Registry cutover is provenance, not an emission cutoff.",
    "The v1.1 12-hour round and separate 24-hour charter cap window must not be conflated. Retained licensesPerDay and LicensesPerDaySet names describe round supply; source-level exact window math and payment split remain unverified. Current status requires live snapshot.py auctions reads, not this historical catalog.",
    "An ABI does not prove where consideration goes, whether it is burned or distributed, or holder yield.",
    "history.py scans these reviewed auction events within explicit finite budgets; treasury buyback events use a separate catalog. Historical RPC availability and coverage must be established for each request; receipt-level Central Bank corroboration remains outside the helper."
  ]
